  "description": "Scans the production accumulator unified_iterative_correction(Z, N) in Z at fixed A (A = 3..8, every Z, k_exact = 4..9), at the proton pin, convention D, mpmath end to end, reading the gated and ungated totals as mpf from the per-step rows so the producer's float64 boundary cast is never taken. The UIC word is the ALL-PAIRS layout, on which any census-linear functional is exactly quadratic in Z, so the discriminator is the THIRD difference, not the second. Measured: Delta^3_Z != 0 in every cell, gated AND ungated, so the per-block log is genuinely outside the additive class of PR #7223 -- the gate is not the cause. Mechanism, exact: the two-branch block trace obeys T2(d1,d2) - T(d1)T(d2) = wPlus(q), independent of both bond offsets, and log|tr_n| factorises through one multiplicative statistic. But there is no valley of stability: argmax_Z never tracks N = Z and is not stable under k_exact, and the all-pairs symmetry curvature L_pp + L_nn - 2 L_pn is POSITIVE, i.e. the additive part makes symmetric nuclei the LEAST bound. Nothing fitted; AME unused.",
