  "caveats": [
    "k_exact = 10 and the producer's default 11 are NOT run over the grid: cost rises ~10x per level (measured: A=6 takes 0.04 s at k=6, 1.2 s at k=8, 11.2 s at k=9), so the 39-cell grid at k=11 is ~12 h. What is reported is the verdict at k_exact = 4..9 and its stability across those six truncations. The Delta^3 != 0 finding is unanimous across all six; the argmax instability is itself one of the findings, so a higher tier could move argmax again but cannot make it stable retroactively.",
    "The exact defect identity of S2 and the factorisation of S3 are proved for a TWO-BRANCH block (two distinct crossing eigenvalues on one generator) -- the twoStrandTrace of ChainTraceFactor. The UIC's general lambda-block spreads crossings over several generators via the cyclic map, where the matrices do not commute and the two-branch form does not apply. S2/S3 are the MECHANISM by which a per-block log can leave the additive class, not a closed form for the production accumulator.",
    "The production functional returns NEGATIVE binding for every cell scanned, reproducing docs/audits/2026-09-05-uic-sign-forced-by-gate.md. This probe does not re-open that; it is noted so no reader takes an argmax over negative numbers for a binding-energy prediction.",
    "The content block unified-iterative-correction.md and the producer DISAGREE on the functional in three ways (no resolvent factor, u_lambda named as an LP shadow price the producer's own docstring disclaims, and no Pass-2 gate in the block at all). The producer is what is scanned here, since it is what runs. Reported as a finding in the audit, not resolved."
  ],
